@Tutorials(name: "Siri AI") {
    @Intro(title: "From SiriKit to Siri AI") {
        Learn SiriKit, App Intents, schemas, Apple Intelligence and the Siri AI Developer Preview
        by building the Memo app's code a few lines per step.
        The material is Apple's official documentation (some of it saved under `docs/apple-doc/`) and WWDC26 sessions.
        At the end of each tutorial there's a prompt for having Claude Code implement the chapter and run it to check.
        As you finish each chapter, paste its prompt and carry on through the implementation.

        Created by Opus 5.5 with Dan Akiyama ([@akidon0000](https://github.com/akidon0000))

        If you find a mistake or something missing, feel free to open a PR at [akidon0000/siri-ai-tutorials](https://github.com/akidon0000/siri-ai-tutorials).
    }

    @Chapter(name: "Chapter 1: From SiriKit to App Intents") {
        @Image(source: "chapter1.svg", alt: "Chapter 1 illustration")

        Write SiriKit's resolve, confirm and handle, then rewrite the same action with App Intents.
        Also learn how apps that used SiriKit custom intents migrate.

        @TutorialReference(tutorial: "doc:01-sirikit-to-app-intents")
    }

    @Chapter(name: "Chapter 2: App Intents basics") {
        @Image(source: "chapter2.svg", alt: "Chapter 2 illustration")

        Expose your app's data and actions to the system with four pieces:
        App Entity, Entity Query, App Enum and App Intent.

        @TutorialReference(tutorial: "doc:02-app-intents-basics")
    }

    @Chapter(name: "Chapter 3: Fix phrases with App Shortcuts") {
        @Image(source: "chapter3.svg", alt: "Chapter 3 illustration")

        Register the phrases people say with AppShortcutsProvider, and point them out inside the app with SiriTipView.

        @TutorialReference(tutorial: "doc:03-app-shortcuts")
    }

    @Chapter(name: "Chapter 4: Design the conversation with Siri") {
        @Image(source: "chapter4.svg", alt: "Chapter 4 illustration")

        Covers the words of responses, follow-up questions, confirmation before running and ownership, static and interactive snippets,
        Siri AI cards (iOS 27.3 beta), and the HIG's guidance on response text.

        @TutorialReference(tutorial: "doc:04-siri-conversation")
    }

    @Chapter(name: "Chapter 5: Bring your app to Apple Intelligence with schemas") {
        @Image(source: "chapter5.svg", alt: "Chapter 5 illustration")

        Choose a fitting domain from App schema domains and fit Memo to the Reminders schemas.
        Also covers migrating without breaking existing shortcuts, in-app search, and the Japan-only side button launch.

        @TutorialReference(tutorial: "doc:05-app-schemas")
    }

    @Chapter(name: "Chapter 6: Give Apple Intelligence context") {
        @Image(source: "chapter6.svg", alt: "Chapter 6 illustration")

        Tell Siri "which memo we're talking about" with Spotlight's semantic index, annotations on screens and notifications,
        donations of UI actions, Transferable, and visual intelligence.

        @TutorialReference(tutorial: "doc:06-apple-intelligence-context")
    }

    @Chapter(name: "Chapter 7: Siri AI Developer Preview [iOS 27.3 beta]") {
        @Image(source: "chapter7.svg", alt: "Chapter 7 illustration")

        Turn actions that no schema covers into tools with `@AppIntent(.tool)`, and use GenerableEntity and
        app skills to let Siri handle complex requests.

        @TutorialReference(tutorial: "doc:07-siri-ai-tools")
    }

    @Chapter(name: "Chapter 8: Verify your implementation") {
        @Image(source: "chapter8.svg", alt: "Chapter 8 illustration")

        Write App Intents Testing integration tests, check by hand in Shortcuts and Spotlight,
        and automate conversation tests with Siri Evaluations (iOS 27.3 beta).

        @TutorialReference(tutorial: "doc:08-verification")
    }
}
